# counter harness. One force call is one evaluation of the squared-error loss and its gradient.
# The network is the PyAMFF 10-7 tanh model. Initial weights are uniform[-1, 1).
# A start that first meets the stop on the call at the cap is a cap failure.
# L-BFGS counts each zoom line-search evaluation. The RMSE at the accepted point is a verification call.
# Default row. L-BFGS keeps 10 vector pairs and takes its step from the Optax zoom line search. Each line-search evaluation counts. Energy coefficient 1 and force coefficient 0.1. The gradient tolerance is 0.1 and the cap is 30000 calls. The network is the PyAMFF 10-7 tanh model on the Behler-Parrinello fingerprints of the EMT Pt 38 trajectory. The loss is the PyAMFF squared error. A start stops when every parameter gradient component is below the tolerance, or when the energy RMSE is below 0.0001 and the force RMSE is below 0.01. One harness call is one evaluation of that loss and its gradient. Initial weights are uniform[-1, 1) from jax.random.key(20261018 + start). A start that first meets the stop on the call at the cap is a cap failure.
problem mlopt/emt-pt38
template optax/emt-pt38-lbfgs-force
cap 30000
counter harness
code Optax
code_version 0.2.8
commit 107e9ad20ca62bcbee1a8c016daab71c690a678c
tuning default
algorithm LBFGS
